    "created_at": "2023-06-01T09:18:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-06-01T09:18:19Z",
    "body": "I've found a bit more background on this. @wjmaclean has been looking into about:blank URL inheritance, mostly for iframes, but he also plans to work on it for popups. See [this Chromium doc](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1e7T1YR5aGDg-eGHKDNnKUWcz1Dr38t_O0-XJqsMeZcE/edit?pli=1&resourcekey=0-qCAYJPulnTdo9hV_dPCdhw). This is mostly captured in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/421; in particular see my summary in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/421#issuecomment-1260360824.\r\n\r\nThis might also explain why Simon and I saw different results, if Simon was testing with experimental web platform features on in his Chrome Canary, or if these changes are rolling out to 50% or similar (which is pretty common on Canary channel).\r\n\r\nIt seems like there is a separate issue here where `open()` and `open(\"about:blank\")` are not treated the same in Firefox.\r\n\r\nI will file a Chromium issue to help @wjmaclean remember to write web platform tests for the popup cases in addition to the iframe cases which he's [already written tests for](https://wpt.fyi/results/html/infrastructure/urls/terminology-0?label=experimental&label=master&aligned).\r\n\r\nWith this in mind, let me close this issue and re-title #421 to also mention popups.",
